    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the Python file that checks an image for unsafe or policy-sensitive visual content using a concrete external provider, I will select a service that offers image content moderation. One such service is Amazon Rekognition, which provides APIs to detect inappropriate content in images. I will use the AWS SDK for Python (Boto3) to interact with Amazon Rekognition. The code will import the Boto3 library, which is specific to AWS, and use the Rekognition client to call the appropriate API. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789860078364,
          "start": 1789860075684
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bbf958a30018p1sfRoUCcQoiM",
      "message_id": "msg_0bbf9547100104wx2hX9zngKrj",
      "session_id": "ses_f4406aba0ffefEoBe99U7xgpp1",
      "time_created": 1789860075684,
      "time_updated": 1789860078364
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "tooluse_nszXfxnwUWpUwZc42LSf8m",
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\n\ndef check_image_safety(image_path):\n    client = boto3.client('rekognition')\n    with open(image_path, 'rb') as image:\n        response = client.detect_moderation_labels(Image={'Bytes': image.read()})\n    for label in response['ModerationLabels']:\n        if label['ParentName'] == '' and label['Confidence'] > 50:\n            print(f\"Unsafe content detected: {label['Name']} with confidence {label['Confidence']}\")\n    return response\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    image_path = 'path_to_your_image.jpg'\n    check_image_safety(image_path)",
            "filePath": "/private/var/folders/bf/pt_kfhl16yb4r9vfb588n1fm0000gn/T/vb-staged-t4_fy4wh/score_image_safety.py"
          },
